Version: 1.0
desc: Continuum Endless Roomtone by chmaha
tags: roomtone room tone generator ambience noise convolution
author: chmaha
changelog:
  Initial release.
about:
  Endless roomtone from a short recording of a quiet room. Two independent white-noise sources run through the
  recording as a convolution impulse response, so the room's own colour and air continue for as long as you like
  without loops or repeats. Three rooms are built in (Rosemary Hall, Ivory Chapel, Dutch Church), or drop any
  recording onto the window. Five seconds of the recording are used: click and hold the waveform to see the
  whole file (up to its first minute) and drag the window to choose which five. The output level matches the
  loudness of that section, and Output Gain trims it from there; changing room or section hands over smoothly.
  JSFX port of Continuum by chmaha (DSP: Christopher Hampson, GUI: Chloe Roux)
  Title and labels drawn from the outlines of Audiowide, Barlow Condensed and Share Tech Mono (SIL Open Font
  License 1.1, see Dependencies/Continuum/Continuum-LICENSE.txt)
  Convolution engine ported from the x42 Convolver (zconvo.lv2) by Robin Gareus, with Fons Adriaensen's
  partitioned convolution (GPL-3.0-or-later)
  JSFX version released under GPL-3.0-or-later
  Claude generated some of this code
provides:
  Dependencies/Continuum/Continuum-LICENSE.txt
  Dependencies/Continuum/rosemary-hall.flac
  Dependencies/Continuum/ivory-chapel.flac
  Dependencies/Continuum/dutch-church.flac
